WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.424 --> 00:00:03.847
Unit twenty-one. Robots Around Us!

2
00:00:04.805 --> 00:00:10.008
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.058 --> 00:00:13.501
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.551 --> 00:00:17.616
Today we learn about Robots Around Us. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:22.592
Robot. Say it with me. Robot!

6
00:00:26.082 --> 00:00:30.115
Machine. Say it with me. Machine!

7
00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:37.184
Move. Say it with me. Move!

8
00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:44.514
Sensor. Say it with me. Sensor!

9
00:00:48.064 --> 00:00:51.825
Help. Say it with me. Help!

10
00:00:55.252 --> 00:00:58.852
Toy. Say it with me. Toy!

11
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.486
Vacuum. Say it with me. Vacuum!

12
00:01:09.986 --> 00:01:13.803
Program. Say it with me. Program!

13
00:01:17.299 --> 00:01:29.851
A robot is a machine that can move and do jobs. Some robots are toys, and some, like a robot vacuum, help clean the house. A robot uses a sensor and follows its program.

14
00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:33.778
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:34.755 --> 00:01:40.271
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.321 --> 00:01:41.471
Move!

17
00:01:42.287 --> 00:01:47.748
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:47.798 --> 00:01:48.948
Vacuum!

19
00:01:50.162 --> 00:01:57.895
Did you know? Many robot vacuums use sensors to avoid bumping into walls and falling down stairs!

20
00:01:57.945 --> 00:02:00.559
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:09.281
Think and answer. What job would you like a robot to do?

22
00:02:09.331 --> 00:02:10.481
Great answer!

23
00:02:11.419 --> 00:02:16.906
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:16.956 --> 00:02:20.050
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

